From dcc4df169be7dddc3e3f8bff15eecf7c1eeb2698 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:21:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: j716s: Build in netfilter, policy routing and
 container support

The J716s root has no modules, so everything a desktop needs from the
network stack has to be =y. The current .config has nf_tables as a bare
core with NF_NAT, NF_CONNTRACK (=m), the nft expressions and
IP_ADVANCED_ROUTER all missing, which leaves ufw, iptables-nft, Docker,
Podman and Tailscale's exit-node and subnet-router mode without the
kernel parts they use. Add them, replacing the two lines (NF_TABLES=y,
NFT_COMPAT=m) the fragment had.

- Policy routing: IP_ADVANCED_ROUTER, IP_MULTIPLE_TABLES and
  IPV6_MULTIPLE_TABLES. Tailscale's router installs ip rules that send
  traffic to table 52; without them it has nothing to hook into.

- WIREGUARD: wg-quick and Tailscale's kernel WireGuard path. Selects
  NET_UDP_TUNNEL (was =m, NET_IP_TUNNEL follows) and the Curve25519,
  Poly1305 and ChaCha20-Poly1305 library code, all built in.

- nftables: NF_TABLES (core already =y) with the INET, IPV4 and IPV6
  families and the CT, NAT, MASQ, REJECT, LIMIT, LOG and FIB
  expressions; NF_NAT with its masquerade helper and the FTP helper;
  NF_CONNTRACK (was =m) with connmark and the FTP helper plus
  CT_NETLINK so conntrack(8) works. NFT_COUNTER has no option any more,
  it is part of nf_tables. These are the same symbols as the
  integration tree's omarchy-desktop.config (b6b0170984cd), minus its
  zram, PWM, schedutil, PM and lockup-detector parts, which the series
  carries or does not want.

- iptables-nft: NFT_COMPAT (was =m) with NETFILTER_XTABLES and the
  match/target extensions the ufw rule files, Docker and Tailscale use:
  mark and connmark, conntrack, state, addrtype, comment, multiport,
  limit, recent, hl, pkttype, LOG, MASQUERADE and the SNAT/DNAT target.
  IP_NF_IPTABLES, IP_NF_TARGET_REJECT and IP6_NF_{IPTABLES,
  TARGET_REJECT,MATCH_IPV6HEADER,MATCH_RT} are there because iptables-nft
  loads ipt_REJECT and the IPv6 rule matches through the xtables
  modules; the legacy filter/nat/mangle tables stay off.

- Containers: VETH, BRIDGE with BRIDGE_NETFILTER (bridged container
  traffic goes through the firewall), OVERLAY_FS and FUSE_FS (overlay
  storage and rootless mounts, Flatpak). TUN, BPF_SYSCALL, CGROUP_BPF,
  the namespaces and the other cgroup controllers are already =y.

Nothing here touches a driver for an Apple block or the boot path. With
defconfig, asahi.config and j716s.config the resolved .config differs
from the previous one only in these options and what they select.
Booted on the J716s (alone, and with the haptic and kernel crypto
fragments): nft works and ip rule lists the local table.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config | 74 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 71 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config b/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
index 3e9078f72154..0a467619560f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
@@ -69,11 +69,79 @@ CONFIG_BT_HCICENTAURI=y
 # runs the suspend path and resumes on its own after 5 s
 CONFIG_PM_DEBUG=y
 
-# Userspace: pacman's download sandbox, nftables, compressed swap, /dev/mem
+# Userspace: pacman's download sandbox, compressed swap, /dev/mem
 CONFIG_SECURITY_LANDLOCK=y
-CONFIG_NF_TABLES=y
-CONFIG_NFT_COMPAT=m
 CONFIG_ZRAM=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM_BACKEND_ZSTD=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_ZSTD=y
 CONFIG_DEVMEM=y
+
+# Desktop networking (the root has no modules, so all of it is built in).
+# Policy routing: Tailscale's router installs ip rules and table 52
+CONFIG_IP_ADVANCED_ROUTER=y
+CONFIG_IP_MULTIPLE_TABLES=y
+CONFIG_IPV6_MULTIPLE_TABLES=y
+
+# WireGuard in the kernel (Tailscale, wg-quick)
+CONFIG_WIREGUARD=y
+
+# nftables, its NAT and conntrack, and the xtables compat layer that
+# iptables-nft (ufw, Docker, Podman, Tailscale) goes through
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_IPTABLES=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_MATCH_IPV6HEADER=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_MATCH_RT=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_TARGET_REJECT=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_IPTABLES=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_TARGET_REJECT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_ADVANCED=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_INGRESS=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XTABLES=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_CONNMARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_COMMENT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_CONNTRACK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_HL=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_MULTIPORT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_PKTTYPE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_RECENT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_STATE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_NAT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_LOG=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MASQUERADE=y
+CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK=y
+CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK_FTP=y
+CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NF_CT_NETLINK=y
+CONFIG_NF_LOG_SYSLOG=y
+CONFIG_NF_NAT=y
+CONFIG_NF_NAT_FTP=y
+CONFIG_NF_NAT_MASQUERADE=y
+CONFIG_NF_REJECT_IPV4=y
+CONFIG_NF_REJECT_IPV6=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES_INET=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES_IPV4=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES_IPV6=y
+CONFIG_NFT_COMPAT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_CT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_INET=y
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_IPV4=y
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_IPV6=y
+CONFIG_NFT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_LOG=y
+CONFIG_NFT_MASQ=y
+CONFIG_NFT_NAT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_REJECT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_REJECT_INET=y
+
+# Containers: veth pairs, a bridge with netfilter, overlayfs, FUSE
+# (rootless Podman, Docker, Flatpak)
+CONFIG_BRIDGE=y
+CONFIG_BRIDGE_NETFILTER=y
+CONFIG_FUSE_FS=y
+CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y
+CONFIG_VETH=y
-- 
